vis[0] = true;
```

Neighbors of `0` are `[1, 2]`.

The first neighbor is `1`, so recursively call:

```
dfs(adj, 1, vis, al);
```

State:

```
Visited = {0}
Result  = [0]
```

### Step 2: Visit vertex 1

Add `1` and mark it visited.

Neighbors of `1` are `[0, 3, 4]`.

| Neighbor | Visited?        | Action                 |
| -------- | --------------- | ---------------------- |
| 0        | Yes             | Skip                   |
| 3        | No              | Recursively visit 3    |
| 4        | Not checked yet | Wait until DFS returns |

Now enter:

```
dfs(adj, 3, vis, al);
```

